the Lord. He himself created her;
he saw her and numbered her
and poured her out over all his works,

He saw her and numbered her;{h}
she rained down knowledge and discerning understanding,
and raised high the glory of those who hold her fast.

Let us fall into the hands of the Lord
and not into human hands;
for as his greatness is,
so too is his mercy.{c}

on the day of your affliction it will be remembered for you;
like fair weather on frost,
so your sins will dissolve.

And do not say, “His compassion is great;
he will atone for the mass of my sins”;
for mercy and wrath are both with him,
and his rage settles upon sinners.

Do not wait to turn back to the Lord,
and do not keep putting it off from day to day;
for suddenly the Lord's wrath will burst out,
and in the time of punishment you will be wiped out.

Do not winnow in every wind,
and do not walk down every path;
that is what the double-tongued sinner does.

Do not get called a whisperer,
and do not set ambushes with your tongue;
for shame falls on the thief,
and harsh condemnation on the double-tongued.

And do not become an enemy instead of a friend;
for a bad name inherits shame and reproach;
that is the way of the double-tongued sinner.

Come to her like one who plows and sows,
and wait for her good fruits;
for in tilling her you will labor a little,
and soon you will eat of her yield.

Do not pick a fight with a hot-tempered man,
and do not cross the wilderness in his company;
for blood counts as nothing in his eyes,
and where there is no help he will strike you down.

Keep far from a man who has power to kill,
and you will not be haunted by the fear of death;
and if you approach him, make no false step,
or he may take away your life;
know that you are walking among snares
and strolling on the battlements of a city.

Do not boast of the wrapping of your garments,
and do not exalt yourself on a day of glory;
for the works of the Lord are wonders,
and his works are hidden from human beings.

Child, do not let your dealings be about many things;
if you multiply them, you will not go clear;
if you chase, you will not catch up,
and if you run off, you will not escape.

Do not wonder at the works of a sinner;
trust in the Lord and keep at your labor;
for it is a light thing in the Lord's eyes
swiftly, in a moment, to make a poor man rich.

Do good to the lowly,
and do not give to the ungodly;
hold back his loaves and do not give them to him,
so that he does not gain the upper hand over you by them;
for you will meet double evil
for all the good you do him.

Has he need of you? He will lead you astray
and smile at you and give you hope;
he will speak fair words to you and say, “What is your need?”

Do not venture to talk with him as an equal,
and do not believe his abundant words;
for by much talk he will test you,
and while smiling he will scrutinize you.

[When you hear this while asleep, rouse yourself;
love the Lord every day you live,
and call to him to save you.]{b}

When a rich man trips, there are many to take his part;
he utters unspeakable things, and they declare him right.
A lowly man trips, and they rebuke him on top of it;
he gives voice to good sense, and no room is given him.

Do not put your trust in their life,
and do not rely on their place;{a}
for one is better than a thousand,
and to die childless than to have ungodly children.

Even if there is one stiff-necked man,
it would be a wonder if he goes unpunished;
for mercy and wrath are both with him;
he is a potentate in forgiving and in pouring out wrath.

[They were given the use of the five powers of the Lord;
for a sixth he granted them a share of mind,
and for a seventh, speech, the interpreter of his powers.]{b}

[He steers the world by the span of his hand,
and all things obey his will;
for he is king of all things by his might,
setting apart among them the holy from the common.]{b}

He will give little and reproach much,
and he will open his mouth like a town crier;
today he will lend, and tomorrow he will ask it back;
a hateful man is such a one.

A fool will say, “I have no friend,
and there are no thanks for my good deeds;
those who eat my bread are evil of tongue.”

As from the face of a snake, flee from sin;
for if you go near, it will bite you;
its teeth are a lion's teeth,
slaying the souls of people.

Do not multiply talk with a senseless man,
and do not go along with one who has no understanding;
guard yourself from him, so that you have no trouble
and are not smeared when he shakes himself;
turn aside from him, and you will find rest
and will not be worn out by his madness.

Stakes standing on a height{b}
will not hold against the wind;
just so, a cowering heart, with a fool's thoughts,
will not hold against any fear.

O Lord, Father and Master of my life,
do not leave me to their counsel;
do not let me fall by them.

A man of many oaths will be filled with lawlessness,
and the whip will not leave his house;
if he offends, his sin is on him,
and if he overlooks it, he has sinned twice;
and if he has sworn idly, he will not be declared righteous,
for his house will be filled with calamities.

For first, she disobeyed the law of the Most High;
second, she offended against her husband;
third, she committed adultery in fornication
and produced children by a strange man.

And those left behind will recognize
that nothing is better than the fear of the Lord
and nothing sweeter than to heed the commandments of the Lord.{b}

[I am mother of beautiful love and of fear,
of knowledge and of holy hope;
everlasting, I am given to all my children,
to those he has named.]{c}

All these things are the book of the covenant of God Most High,
a law that Moses commanded us,
an inheritance for the gatherings of Jacob.{d}

[Do not grow faint in being strong in the Lord;
hold fast to him, that he may give you strength;
the Lord Almighty is God alone,
and there is no savior other than he.]

Nine notions I count blessed in my heart,
and the tenth I will utter with my tongue:
a man gladdened by his children;
one who lives to see the fall of his enemies;

blessed is he who dwells with a wife of understanding,
and he who has not slipped with his tongue,{b}
and he who has not served someone unworthy of him;

As is the wood of the fire, so it will blaze;
and as is the stubbornness of strife, so it will blaze;
as a man's strength is, so will his wrath be,
and in proportion to his riches he will raise his anger.

If you blow on a spark, it will flare,
and if you spit on it, it will go out;
and both come out of your mouth.

If he can pay, the lender will scarcely get half
and will count it a windfall;
if not, he has been robbed of his money
and has gained an enemy for nothing;
curses and abuse are the repayment he gets,
and instead of glory, dishonor.

Coax your soul and comfort your heart,
and drive grief far away from you;
for grief has destroyed many,
and there is no profit in it.

Remember that an evil eye is a wicked thing.{b}
What has been created more wicked than an eye?
That is why it sheds tears at every turn.

Have they made you master of the feast? Do not be lifted up;
be among them as one of them;
take care of them, and then sit down.

Opposite evil stands the good,
and opposite death, life;
so opposite the godly stands the sinner.

and do not lean on an unrighteous sacrifice;
for the Lord is judge,
and with him there is no favor to persons.

The prayer of a humble man goes right through the clouds,
and until it draws near he will not be comforted;
he will not leave off until the Most High looks upon him

and paid back vengeance to the nations,
until he has taken away the crowd of the insolent
and broken to pieces the scepters of the unrighteous;

So it is with every craftsman and master builder
who passes the night as he does the day;
those who cut the engravings of seals,
whose patience is in varying the pattern;
he will give his heart to making the likeness exact,
and his wakefulness to finishing the work.

So the smith, sitting beside the anvil
and studying the iron he works;
the breath of the fire will melt his flesh,
and in the heat of the furnace he wrestles;
the noise of the hammer deafens his ear,{e}
and his eyes are on the pattern of the vessel;
he will give his heart to finishing his works,
and his wakefulness to adorning them to completion.

Yet they will not be sought out for the council of the people,
and in the assembly they will not rise high;
they will not sit on the judge's seat,
and they will not understand the covenant of judgment;

like frankincense give off a sweet smell,
and blossom like a lily;
spread your fragrance and sing a song of praise;
bless the Lord for all his works.

Therefore feel shame as my word directs,
for it is not good to keep every kind of shame,
and not everything is approved by all in good faith.

before a partner and a friend of injustice,
and before the place where you sojourn of theft,
and before the truth of God and the covenant;
and of leaning your elbow on the bread,{b}

of contempt in taking and giving;
before those who greet you, of silence;
of gazing at a prostitute;

of turning away the face of your kinsman,
of taking away a portion and a gift;
of staring at a married woman;

I will now call to mind the works of the Lord,
and what I have seen I will tell.
By the words of the Lord his works came to be.{d}

A man blowing a furnace works in burning heat;
three times as much the sun scorches mountains;
breathing out fiery vapors
and flashing out its rays, it dims the eyes.

When you glorify the Lord, lift him up as far as you can,
for he will surpass even that;
and when you lift him up, gather your strength;
do not grow weary, for you will never reach the end.

leaders of the people by their counsels
and by their understanding of the people's learning,
wise in the words of their instruction;

Noah was found perfect, righteous;
in the season of wrath he became a replacement;{c}
on his account a remnant was left on the earth
when the flood came.

he kept the law of the Most High
and entered into a covenant with him;
in his flesh he set up the covenant,
and when he was tested he was found faithful.{d}

By his words he made the signs cease;{b}
he glorified him in the presence of kings;
he gave him commands for his people
and showed him part of his glory.

He clothed him in the perfection of boasting
and strengthened him with the vestments of might:
the linen undergarments, the long robe, and the ephod.{d}

with a holy robe of gold and blue and purple,
an embroiderer's handiwork;
with the oracle of judgment, the signs of truth,{e}

with twisted scarlet, the work of a craftsman;
with precious stones engraved like seals
in a setting of gold, the work of a jeweler,
as a memorial in engraved writing,
by the number of the tribes of Israel;

Moses filled his hands{h}
and anointed him with holy oil;
it became for him an everlasting covenant,
and for his offspring in the days of heaven,
to minister to the Lord and also to act as priest
and to bless his people in his name.

And he added glory to Aaron
and gave him an inheritance;
he apportioned to him the first fruits of the firstborn;
bread first of all he prepared in abundance;

Yet in the land of the people he will have no inheritance,
and there is no portion for him among the people;
for he himself is your portion and inheritance.{j}

Phinehas son of Eleazar is the third in glory,{k}
for his zeal in the fear of the Lord,
and for standing firm when the people turned away,
in the goodness of his soul's eagerness;
and he made atonement for Israel.

There was also a covenant with David
son of Jesse, of the tribe of Judah:
the king's inheritance passes from son to son alone;
so the inheritance of Aaron is for his offspring.{l}

He called on the Lord, the Mighty One,
when his enemies pressed on him from every side,
with the offering of a suckling lamb.{f}

And before the time of his sleep of the age
he bore witness before the Lord and his anointed:
“Money, or even sandals, from any flesh I have not taken”;
and no one accused him.{h}

And after his falling asleep he still prophesied;
he made known to the king his end
and raised his voice out of the ground in prophecy,
to blot out the people's lawlessness.{i}

So they glorified him for his ten thousands{c}
and praised him in the blessings of the Lord,
when the crown of glory was brought to him.

For he wiped out his enemies all around
and brought to nothing the Philistines, his adversaries;
to this day he has crushed their horn.

The Lord put away his sins{e}
and exalted his horn to the age;
a covenant of kingship he granted him
and a throne of glory in Israel.

You put a blemish on your glory
and profaned your offspring,
bringing wrath upon your children;
and I was grieved over your folly,{h}

But the Lord will never leave off his mercy,
nor will he let any of his words come to ruin;
he will never wipe out the descendants of his chosen one,
nor take away the offspring of the one who loved him;
and he gave Jacob a remnant,
and to David a root from his own stock.

Blessed are those who saw you
and those who have been adorned in love;
for we too shall surely live.{g}

Hezekiah fortified his city
and brought water into its midst;
he dug through sheer rock with iron
and built pools for water.{i}

In his days Sennacherib came up
and sent Rabshakeh, and set out;
he lifted up his hand against Zion
and boasted in his arrogance.{j}

and so was Joshua son of Jozadak;
in their days these built the house
and lifted up a temple holy to the Lord,
made ready for everlasting glory.{g}

Nor was a man born like Joseph,
leader of his brothers, a prop of his people,
and his bones were watched over.{j}

Simon son of Onias,{a} the high priest,
who in his life repaired the house
and in his days made the temple strong;

And when he received the portions from the priests' hands
while he himself stood by the hearth of the altar,
around him was a garland of brothers,
like a young growth of cedars in Lebanon;
and they surrounded him like the trunks of palms,

Then the sons of Aaron shouted out;
they sounded with trumpets of hammered metal;
they made a great sound heard
as a memorial before the Most High.

I will give thanks to you, Lord, King,
and I will praise you, God my Savior;
I give thanks to your name,

for you became my shelter and my help,
and you redeemed my body from destruction
and from the snare of a slandering tongue,
from lips that work out a lie;
and in the face of those who stood by you became my helper,

and you redeemed me, by the abundance of your mercy and of your name,
from the bites of those ready to devour,
from the hand of those seeking my life,
from the many afflictions I had,

I called on the Lord, the Father of my lord,{a}
not to forsake me in the days of affliction,
in the time of the arrogant, when there is no help.

I will praise your name continually
and sing a song of praise in thanksgiving;
and my supplication was heard,

From her blossom, as from a ripening grape, my heart was glad in her;
my foot walked on the level path;
from my youth I followed her track.

Put your neck under the yoke,
and let your soul receive discipline;
she is near at hand to be found.
